-- title:
--   The Young symmetrizer module of a Young diagram is its Specht module
-- statement:
--   Let $\mu$ be a Young diagram with $N$ cells and $t$ a tableau of shape $\mu$ (an enumeration $\{0, \dots, N-1\} \to \mu$ of its cells, `OAI.Saxl.Tableau N μ`). Let $V_\mu$ be the left ideal $\mathbb C[\mathbf S_N]\, c_\mu$ of the group algebra generated by the Young symmetrizer $c_\mu = a_\mu b_\mu$ of the tableau with row lengths $\mu_1 \ge \mu_2 \ge \dots$ filled in order with $0, 1, \dots, N-1$ (`StrongConv.youngSpace N μ.rowLens`), on which $\sigma \in \mathbf S_N$ acts by left multiplication (`StrongConv.youngAct`). Then there is a complex linear isomorphism $e$ from $V_\mu$ to the Specht module $S^t$ of $t$ (`OAI.Saxl.Specht t`) such that $e(\sigma x) = \sigma \cdot e(x)$ for every $\sigma \in \mathbf S_N$ and every $x \in V_\mu$, where $\mathbf S_N$ acts on $S^t$ by `OAI.Saxl.spechtRep t`.
--
--   Here $a_\mu$ is the sum of the permutations preserving every row of that tableau and $b_\mu$ the signed sum of those preserving every column (Fulton–Harris, §4.1), and $S^t$ is the span of the $\mathbf S_N$-translates of the polytabloid of $t$ (James, §4).
--
--   This identifies the representation of $\mathbf S_N$ that the bundle `Def_StrongConvG4` uses for "the irreducible representation of $\mathbf S_N$ defined by" a partition (Chen–Garza-Vargas–Tropp–van Handel, p. 14, for the partitions $\lambda[N]$) with the Specht module of the same shape. Specht modules are irreducible (`OAI.Saxl.specht_irreducible`), and every irreducible representation of $\mathbf S_N$ is isomorphic to one of them (`OAI.Saxl.irreducible_equiv_specht`).
--
--   References: W. Fulton and J. Harris, *Representation Theory: A First Course*, Graduate Texts in Mathematics 129, Springer, 1991, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0979-9, Lecture 4 (Theorem 4.3); G. D. James, *The Representation Theory of the Symmetric Groups*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 682, Springer, 1978, https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0067708.
-- source:
--   Chen, C.-F., Garza-Vargas, J., Tropp, J. A. and van Handel, R., A new approach to strong convergence, Ann. of Math. (2) 203 (2026) 555–602, https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2026.203.2.4 (arXiv:2405.16026v3, whose page numbers are used), p. 14, the irreducible representation of S_N defined by a partition, identified with its Specht module (supporting fact, not in the paper), with Fulton, W. and Harris, J., Representation Theory: A First Course, GTM 129, Springer, 1991, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0979-9, Theorem 4.3, and James, G. D., The Representation Theory of the Symmetric Groups, LNM 682, Springer, 1978, https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0067708

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_StrongConvG4
import Definitions.Def_Saxl

namespace StrongConv

theorem exists_linearEquiv_youngSpace_specht {N : ℕ} {μ : YoungDiagram}
    (t : OAI.Saxl.Tableau N μ) :
    ∃ e : youngSpace N μ.rowLens ≃ₗ[ℂ] OAI.Saxl.Specht t,
      ∀ (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin N)) (x : youngSpace N μ.rowLens),
        e (youngAct N μ.rowLens σ x) = OAI.Saxl.spechtRep t σ (e x) := by
  sorry

end StrongConv
